            # Rate limited - return 429\\n            retry_after = 60  # seconds\\n            self.send_response(429)\\n            self.send_header('Content-Type', 'application/json')\\n            self.send_header('Retry-After', str(retry_after))\\n            self.send_header('Content-Length', '12')\\n            self.end_headers()\\n            self.wfile.write(json.dumps({\\\"error\\\": \\\"Rate limit exceeded\\\"}).encode())\\n\\n        # Record this request\\n        with self.lock:\\n            self.request_history[client_ip].append(now)\\n\\n\\nPORT = 8000\\n\\nwith socketserver.TCPServer((\\\"\\\", PORT), RateLimitedHandler) as httpd:\\n    httpd.allow_reuse_address = True\\n    print(f\\\"Serving on http://localhost:{PORT}\\\")\\n    httpd.serve_forever()\\n\", \"path\": \"server.py\"}"}}]}], "recent_messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Build a rate-limited API.\n\nCreate two files:\n\n1. server.py \u2014 HTTP server using only the Python standard library:\n   - GET /api/time returns {\"now\": <unix timestamp>}.\n   - A per-client rate limit of 5 requests per 60 seconds, keyed by client IP.\n   - The 6th and further requests within the window return 429 with a Retry-After header.\n2. throttle.ts \u2014 export function throttle(fn: () => void, maxPerWindow: number, windowMs: number):\n   returns a wrapper that calls fn at most maxPerWindow times per windowMs and silently skips\n   excess calls. Include a brief self-test that passes when run with: node throttle.ts\n\nUse only the Python standard library. Do not install packages.\nVerify before finishing: curl /api/time six times in a row and show that the 6th returns 429.\n\n\nYou are being benchmarked. Work only inside the current working directory.\nUse relative paths for all file operations and commands (e.g. write server.py, run node todos.ts). Never use absolute paths.\nPython code must use only the Python standard library. Package installation is disabled: npm, npx and pip install will be refu